# Line endings are a property of the repository, not of the machine.
#
# `core.autocrlf` lives in the developer's git config and does NOT travel with a
# clone — the same category as the Windows Defender exclusions that CLAUDE.md
# has to write down by hand. This file travels, and it wins over that setting.
#
# Without it, `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into the working tree at checkout
# while .editorconfig (`end_of_line = lf`) and Prettier (`endOfLine: lf`, the
# default) both expect LF. The index was always LF; only the working copy
# diverged — which is why ESLint reported a `Delete ␍` warning on every line of
# every file that had ever been checked out, 485 of them across nine files, with
# nothing actually wrong in the repository.
*                text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalised, never diffed as text. `text=auto` already detects
# these, but naming them means a corrupt icon can never be one heuristic away.
*.png            binary
*.ico            binary
*.icns           binary
